      {
        "id": 214246,
        "name": "lynkfox",
        "username": "lynkfox",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-31T22:54:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm not entirely certain the best way, but I'd put all the Spirit Panels and their tokens (in baggies) in the Branch and Claw box, anbd everything else (Using baggies that came with the box for the tokens/invaders/ect) in the main. That way you can hand the branch and claw box around to players to pick spirits while someone else uses the other box to set up.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I might get a small cardboard cardbox for the cards - you can get one for a dollar or two usually at any game store, and that would work really nicely for the cards.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:45:24.181Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
